   "spatialCue": "straight ahead, about 800 feet",
   "text": "Straight ahead, about 800 feet: National September 11 Memorial & Museum. The National September 11 Memorial & Museum honors the victims of the September 11, 2001 attacks and of the 1993 World Trade Center bombing. The memorial, titled Reflecting Absence, was designed by Michael Arad with landscape architects Peter Walker and Partners. The memorial opened on September 11, 2011, and the museum was dedicated on May 15, 2014. The names of 2,983 victims are inscribed on 152 bronze parapets around the memorial pools. The two memorial pools sit in the footprints of the original Twin Towers. That's the story.",
